From: Doruk Aktun <info@dorukaktun.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: hi556: add a device tree match

The Hi-556 is also used on Qualcomm phones described by device tree (the
Razer Edge's front camera, SM8350). Supplies and the reset GPIO are already
looked up by name, so add the match table.

The clock is requested by the name "clk", which only works on ACPI, where
a fixed clock is registered for the sensor. A device tree node with a
single clock has no clock-names, so look the clock up without a name, as
the other single-clock sensor drivers do.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/hi556.c b/drivers/media/i2c/hi556.c
index de573ce..8b9a77c 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/hi556.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/hi556.c
@@ -1341,7 +1341,7 @@ static int hi556_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 		return dev_err_probe(hi556->dev, PTR_ERR(hi556->reset_gpio),
 				     "failed to get reset GPIO\n");
 
-	hi556->clk = devm_v4l2_sensor_clk_get(hi556->dev, "clk");
+	hi556->clk = devm_v4l2_sensor_clk_get(hi556->dev, NULL);
 	if (IS_ERR(hi556->clk))
 		return dev_err_probe(hi556->dev, PTR_ERR(hi556->clk),
 				     "failed to get clock\n");
@@ -1437,10 +1437,17 @@ static const struct acpi_device_id hi556_acpi_ids[] = {
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(acpi, hi556_acpi_ids);
 #endif
 
+static const struct of_device_id hi556_of_match[] = {
+	{ .compatible = "hynix,hi556" },
+	{ }
+};
+MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, hi556_of_match);
+
 static struct i2c_driver hi556_i2c_driver = {
 	.driver = {
 		.name = "hi556",
 		.acpi_match_table = ACPI_PTR(hi556_acpi_ids),
+		.of_match_table = hi556_of_match,
 		.pm = pm_sleep_ptr(&hi556_pm_ops),
 	},
 	.probe = hi556_probe,
